hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"5","Ali bin Hajar Al-Saadi told us, Ismail, meaning Ibn Jafar, told us, Al-Alaa, who is Ibn Abd al-Rahman, told us. H, Bishr bin Muadh Al-Aqdi told us, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, Ruh bin Al-Qasim told us, Al-Ala’ told us. H Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Ibn Wahb told us, that Malik told him, on the authority of Al-Ala bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not guide you to that by which God erases sins and raises ranks?!” They said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “Performing ablution thoroughly in the case of hardship, taking many steps to the mosques, and waiting for prayer after prayer. That is the bond, that is the bond.” One word, except that Ali bin Hajar said: That is the bond once, and Yunus said in his hadith: Shall I not inform you of what God erases sins with? He did not say: They said: Yes"
